        1300
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 17,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Reprise \u2014 where can words live in this shot?\n\n**Reprise** puts lyrics and captions *inside* real footage: behind the person, on the wall, following the head, reframed for vertical. This graph runs every analysis the Reprise editor uses, on one clip and one song, all local and deterministic:\n\n1. **Footage** \u2192 frames + fps (`typeset_walk_night.mp4` in your input folder).\n2. **BiRefNet** cuts out the subject (MASK).\n3. **Occupancy Grid** \u2014 per frame, how much of each cell the subject covers. Reprise places `behind` text where it stays readable. Red = subject, green = free.\n4. **Mask \u2192 Tracks \u2192 Reframe Crop** \u2014 a dead-zone, critically damped virtual camera that follows the head; the saved video is the 9:16 crop.\n5. **Planar Track** \u2014 a quad drawn on the roller shutter at frame 70 is tracked forwards and backwards with homographies while the person walks through it (masked out). The JSON is what the renderer uses to warp text onto the wall.\n6. **Beat Grid** (beats, downbeats, sections) and **Whisper Words** with lyric alignment (`typeset_neon_rain.flac`): exact lyric spelling, sung timing.\n\nNodes: `typeset_nodes` (MIT). Every JSON output matches docs/SCHEMA.md and feeds the Reprise renderer directly."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
